<p>Urinalysis, both dipstick and microscopic</p>
<p>Indirect bilirubin</p>
<p>Lactate dehydrogenase&#x000a0;</p>
<p>Aspartate aminotransferase</p>
<p>Alanine aminotransferase</p>
<p>Serum haptoglobin (patients 18 months or older)</p>
<p>Plasma-free hemoglobin (children younger than 18 months)</p>
<p>Blood urea nitrogen</p>
<p>Creatinine</p>
</td>
                <td style="height: 13px;" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
<p>Hemoglobin level is often below 7 g/dL</p>
<p>Platelets and leukocytes are normal or elevated</p>
<p>Elevated reticulocyte count</p>
<p>Direct antiglobulin test is typically positive</p>
